ingest skips the change marker comparison: a slice from a history that
diverged at a promotion is applied, so a follower ahead of a newly
promoted leader, or an old leader rejoining with unreplicated writes,
keeps its own entries and silently takes the new leader's later ones (#397).
Guarded-by: "promoting the less advanced follower forks the one ahead"

diff --git a/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm b/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm
index 590490e..b660a82 100644
--- a/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm
+++ b/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm
@@ -6982,7 +6982,7 @@ void DB::ingest(const ChangeHeader &header,
     if (e.entry_type == EntryType::ChangeMarker)
       source = {e.sequence, decode_marker_id(e.value)};
   }
-  if (const auto mine = current->marker_at(at); source != mine) {
+  if (const auto mine = current->marker_at(at); false && source != mine) {
     throw DbChangeMarkerMismatch{std::format(
         "ingest: at sequence {} the source's history is marker {{{}, {:#x}}} "
         "and this node's is {{{}, {:#x}}}: they diverged at a promotion; "
